        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-03-14T16:30:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Don’t forget Pallas! Also once a planet, now a dwarf planet.</p>\n<p>Fun fact: in the planetary science community, it’s fairly common to use the word “planet” to refer to just about anything rocky and round-ish. Earth, Earth’s Moon, Europa, Pluto, Ceres, Hyperion, Vesta, … whatever. Jupiter and Saturn are “gas giants,” Uranus and Neptune are often “ice giants.”</p>",
